<rss version="2.0" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><title>智能新闻| smithsonianmag.com</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/rss/smart-news/</link><description>智能新闻的 RSS 提要</description><lastBuildDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 15:58:36 GMT</lastBuildDate><generator>rfeed v1.1.1</generator><docs>https://github.com/svpino/rfeed/blob/master/README.md</docs><item><title>这只狗学会了嗅出一种被称为“海呕吐物”的粘糊糊的海洋入侵者——这一技能为她赢得了年度动物奖</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-dog-learned-to-sniff-out-a-slimy-marine-invader-called-sea-vomit-a-skill-that-earned-her-the-animal-of-the-year-award-180989706/</link><description>来自苏格兰高地的6岁拉布拉多犬Sgiath获得了国际动物福利基金会颁发的荣誉。据信，她是第一只接受训练来捕猎入侵性地毯海鞘的幼崽，这种海鞘正在威胁英国海岸和其他地方的海洋生物</description><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-dog-learned-to-sniff-out-a-slimy-marine-invader-called-sea-vomit-a-skill-that-earned-her-the-animal-of-the-year-award-180989706/</guid></item><item><title>考古学家在格陵兰岛寻找北欧教堂的证据，在红发埃里克的定居点附近发现了“铁证”</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/archaeologists-searching-for-evidence-of-a-norse-church-in-greenland-have-found-the-smoking-gu-near-erik-the-reds-settlement-180989716/</link><description>几十年前，该地点首次被确定为可能的教堂，但研究人员直到今年夏天在那里发现了人类遗骸才证实了这一预感。它可能为 15 世纪维京人的不明失踪事件提供另一条线索</description><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 11:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/archaeologists-searching-for-evidence-of-a-norse-church-in-greenland-have-found-the-smoking-gu-near-erik-the-reds-settlement-180989716/</guid></item><item><title>法国市政厅的烧毁是一场“遗产灾难”，悲剧性地让人想起巴黎圣母院火灾</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/the-burning-of-this-french-city-hall-was-a-catastrophe-for-heritage-tragically-reminiscent-of-the-notre-dame-fire-180989711/</link><description>法国当局表示，建于 19 世纪末、被誉为建筑瑰宝的利摩日市政厅在周末法国大规模抗议活动中成为纵火袭击的受害者</description><pubDate>Mon, 19 Oct 2026 21:13:51 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/the-burning-of-this-french-city-hall-was-a-catastrophe-for-heritage-tragically-reminiscent-of-the-notre-dame-fire-180989711/</guid></item><item><title>科学家们不知道火星是如何获得它的两个卫星的。日本刚刚启动了一项历史性的太空任务，将采集样本以找出答案</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/scientists-dont-know-how-mars-acquired-its-two-moons-japan-just-launched-a-historic-space-mission-that-will-fetch-samples-to-find-out-180989713/</link><description>日本宇宙航空研究开发机构的宇宙飞船预计将于 2027 年 8 月抵达火星系统，并于 2031 年将火卫一月球样本返回地球</description><pubDate>Mon, 19 Oct 2026 19:41:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/scientists-dont-know-how-mars-acquired-its-two-moons-japan-just-launched-a-historic-space-mission-that-will-fetch-samples-to-find-out-180989713/</guid></item><item><title>当一位 19 世纪的苏格兰地主封锁一条公共人行道时，当地人发起了反抗。现在，考古学家出土了他备受争议的城墙的一部分</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/when-a-19th-century-scottish-landowner-blocked-a-public-footpath-locals-rebelled-now-archaeologists-have-unearthed-parts-of-his-controversial-wall-180989712/</link><description>对“哈维堤”（一对建于 1820 年代的石墙）的反抗是格拉斯哥工人和中产阶级的胜利，他们利用骚乱、抵制和诉讼重新赢得了克莱德河的通行权</description><pubDate>Mon, 19 Oct 2026 19:17:45 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/when-a-19th-century-scottish-landowner-blocked-a-public-footpath-locals-rebelled-now-archaeologists-have-unearthed-parts-of-his-controversial-wall-180989712/</guid></item><item><title>研究表明，地球真正的北极和南极在过去 3.2 亿年里已经漂移了四次</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/earths-true-north-and-south-poles-have-wandered-four-times-over-the-past-320-million-years-study-suggests-180989698/</link><description>这种涉及地理极点的现象与磁极移动时不同。地球的固体地壳和熔融地幔偶尔会发生移动，随后在所谓的真正的极地漂移期间重新调整方向</description><pubDate>Mon, 19 Oct 2026 15:01:46 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/earths-true-north-and-south-poles-have-wandered-four-times-over-the-past-320-million-years-study-suggests-180989698/</guid></item><item><title>科罗拉多州的野生动物减缓工作（包括北美最大的动物过境立交桥）如何让每个人都更安全</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/how-colorados-wildlife-mitigation-efforts-including-the-largest-animal-crossing-overpass-in-north-america-are-making-everyone-safer-180989704/</link><description>得益于围栏、地下通道和大型立交桥等新基础设施，动物现在可以穿越 25 号州际公路的危险路段，这使得野生动物与车辆的碰撞事故减少了 91%</description><pubDate>Mon, 19 Oct 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/how-colorados-wildlife-mitigation-efforts-including-the-largest-animal-crossing-overpass-in-north-america-are-making-everyone-safer-180989704/</guid></item><item><title>埃及的一位农民偶然发现了一块粉红色的石头，并打电话给当局。他们在财产下方发现了拉美西斯二世的两座巨大雕像的遗骸</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-farmer-in-egypt-stumbled-upon-a-pink-stone-and-called-the-authorities-they-found-the-remains-of-two-colossal-statues-of-ramses-ii-beneath-the-property-180989708/</link><description>考古学家发现了一尊雕像的头部，该雕像可能高约 28 英尺。它可能指向法老委托建造的一个主要建筑工地</description><pubDate>Mon, 19 Oct 2026 12:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-farmer-in-egypt-stumbled-upon-a-pink-stone-and-called-the-authorities-they-found-the-remains-of-two-colossal-statues-of-ramses-ii-beneath-the-property-180989708/</guid></item><item><title>伦勃朗将古代神话变成“至高无上的人类”艺术作品。即将举办的展览追溯了他从古代汲取的灵感</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/rembrandt-turned-ancient-myths-into-supremely-human-works-of-art-an-upcoming-exhibition-traces-the-inspiration-he-took-from-antiquity-180989705/</link><description>大都会艺术博物馆的“伦勃朗与古代人”将揭开这位荷兰大师职业生涯中“未被充分探索但至关重要”的部分，将他的画作与启发他们的前世进行对话</description><pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 20:16:08 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/rembrandt-turned-ancient-myths-into-supremely-human-works-of-art-an-upcoming-exhibition-traces-the-inspiration-he-took-from-antiquity-180989705/</guid></item><item><title>传说这位罗马皇帝在威尔士建立了一个营地。新发现的堡垒可能证明它确实存在</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/legend-has-it-that-this-roman-emperor-established-camp-wales-newly-discovered-fort-may-offer-proof-that-it-really-existed-180989702/</link><description>一位考古学家发现了一座与马格努斯·马克西姆斯有关的古代防御工事，马格努斯·马克西姆斯是一位四世纪的统治者，在中世纪的“马比诺吉翁”故事中以 Macsen Wledig 的名字永垂不朽。</description><pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 18:51:49 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/legend-has-it-that-this-roman-emperor-established-camp-wales-newly-discovered-fort-may-offer-proof-that-it-really-existed-180989702/</guid></item><item><title>野生动物专家惊讶地发现禽流感杀死了深受喜爱的网络著名秃头鹰杰基</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/wildlife-experts-stunned-to-find-that-bird-flu-killed-jackie-the-beloved-internet-famous-bald-eagle-180989703/</link><description>杰基在加利福尼亚州奥海猛禽中心接受了数周的重症监护后于八月去世。尸检结果令人惊讶，因为杰基的症状对于禽流感来说并不常见，而且秃鹰之间没有持续爆发疫情</description><pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 18:23:17 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/wildlife-experts-stunned-to-find-that-bird-flu-killed-jackie-the-beloved-internet-famous-bald-eagle-180989703/</guid></item><item><title>马德里翻新扩建的索罗拉博物馆让西班牙“光之大师”的画作重新出现在公众视野中</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/madrids-renewed-and-expanded-sorolla-museum-lets-the-paintings-of-the-spanish-master-of-light-reemerge-into-public-view-180989701/</link><description>该博物馆致力于展示华金·索罗拉·巴斯蒂达 (Joaquín Sorolla y Bastida) 的作品，以他历史悠久的住宅和工作室为中心。历时数年的改造第一阶段已完成，展览空间扩大</description><pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 18:01:39 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/madrids-renewed-and-expanded-sorolla-museum-lets-the-paintings-of-the-spanish-master-of-light-reemerge-into-public-view-180989701/</guid></item><item><title>微塑料与无数人类健康问题有关。科学家可能终于弄清楚它们如何伤害身体</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/microplastics-have-been-linked-with-myriad-human-health-problems-scientists-may-have-finally-figured-out-how-they-harm-the-body-180989694/</link><description>实验室实验表明，微小的塑料碎片可以与我们体内的水发生反应，产生高活性分子。它们会导致破坏性的氧化应激和炎症</description><pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 17:03:22 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/microplastics-have-been-linked-with-myriad-human-health-problems-scientists-may-have-finally-figured-out-how-they-harm-the-body-180989694/</guid></item><item><title>小型犬往往比大型犬活得更长。科学家表示，他们可能终于知道原因了——而且已经深入到分子水平</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/small-dogs-tend-to-live-longer-than-big-dogs-scientists-say-they-might-finally-know-why-and-it-goes-to-the-molecular-level-180989695/</link><description>像大丹犬这样的大型品种似乎比吉娃娃等小型品种更快地在 DNA 上积累化学标签的变化。这些改变允许潜在有害的“跳跃基因”在其基因组中移动</description><pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 16:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/small-dogs-tend-to-live-longer-than-big-dogs-scientists-say-they-might-finally-know-why-and-it-goes-to-the-molecular-level-180989695/</guid></item><item><title>这种古老的动物看起来像鸭嘴兽和水獭的杂交种。它提供了有关哺乳动物哺乳和吞咽起源的线索</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-ancient-animal-looked-like-a-platapys-otter-hybrid-its-providing-clues-about-the-origins-of-mammalian-suckling-and-swallowing-180989666/</link><description>这种重约两到四磅的掠食者在大约 1.65 亿年前与恐龙一起生活。在中国北方发现的化石表明，这种奇怪的生物具有令人惊讶的现代喉咙结构</description><pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-ancient-animal-looked-like-a-platapys-otter-hybrid-its-providing-clues-about-the-origins-of-mammalian-suckling-and-swallowing-180989666/</guid></item><item><title>一幅 18 世纪波利尼西亚年轻人的纪念肖像——一件“最高艺术作品”——首次访问美国</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-monumental-18th-century-portrait-of-a-young-polynesian-man-a-supreme-work-of-art-visits-the-us-for-the-first-time-180989699/</link><description>巨幅《麦肖像》描绘了第一位访问英国的太平洋岛民，这位年轻人在参加探险家詹姆斯·库克的探险队后，在 1770 年代成为准名人</description><pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 12:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-monumental-18th-century-portrait-of-a-young-polynesian-man-a-supreme-work-of-art-visits-the-us-for-the-first-time-180989699/</guid></item><item><title>官方消息：计时员已经摆脱了闰秒，并引入了闰时</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/its-official-timekeepers-have-gotten-rid-of-the-leap-second-and-introduced-the-leap-hour-instead-180989685/</link><description>自 1972 年以来，专家们在协调世界时的基础上增加了 27 秒，以使其与地球自转保持一致，但这并不是一个完美的解决方案</description><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 20:43:52 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/its-official-timekeepers-have-gotten-rid-of-the-leap-second-and-introduced-the-leap-hour-instead-180989685/</guid></item><item><title>在巴黎郊外的一座小岛上，一座被恰如其分地称为“大”的庞大当代艺术中心准备开门迎客</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/on-an-island-outside-paris-a-sprawling-contemporary-arts-center-aptly-called-large-prepares-to-open-its-doors-180989690/</link><description>这个具有里程碑意义的机构的首次展览是为了向曾经在塞纳河塞金岛上运营的历史悠久的雷诺汽车工厂致敬。一位官员表示：“这个项目需要极大的毅力”</description><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 20:19:07 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/on-an-island-outside-paris-a-sprawling-contemporary-arts-center-aptly-called-large-prepares-to-open-its-doors-180989690/</guid></item><item><title>这位士兵在第一次世界大战的战壕里写了一本日记。几十年后，一个孩子在垃圾场发现了它，它被子弹刺穿，沾满血迹</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-soldier-kept-a-diary-in-the-trenches-of-world-war-i-a-child-found-it-at-the-dump-decades-later-pierced-by-a-bullet-and-stained-with-blood-180989696/</link><description>克洛德·纳托尔下士在日记中记录了他的战时经历。现在，经过几十年的研究，一位博物馆馆长在一本新书中讲述了这名士兵的故事</description><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 19:41:46 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-soldier-kept-a-diary-in-the-trenches-of-world-war-i-a-child-found-it-at-the-dump-decades-later-pierced-by-a-bullet-and-stained-with-blood-180989696/</guid></item><item><title>威尼斯艺术家卡纳莱托在这幅前所未见的素描中融合了幻想和建筑细节，本月即将拍卖</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/venetian-artist-canaletto-merged-fantasy-and-architectural-detail-in-this-previously-unseen-sketch-heading-to-auction-this-month-180989692/</link><description>这位 18 世纪的画家是“随想”艺术的主要实践者，这种艺术将日常生活场景与大胆、不合时宜的结构融为一体。这件作品在几个世纪以来一直不为人知，现在售价高达 80,000 美元</description><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 18:03:46 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/venetian-artist-canaletto-merged-fantasy-and-architectural-detail-in-this-previously-unseen-sketch-heading-to-auction-this-month-180989692/</guid></item></channel></rss>